# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 35, with a turn-time check of master after TIME-14/15.
# Round 34 ran as PR #1086 (A/A -0.03 +- 0.07): every line held and was banked (#1088, plans/locks34-shipped.txt):
# Lajcsi2sm gl +1.9, Lynx +5.5, Pris +4.3, Combat +2.4 and Che +1.3 cpl, and the 46-robot rwl class at +0.20 a robot.
# Round 35 carries 12 robots on existing table switches, each read on fresh cloud seeds at 0.7x the live turn time (the
# PC's 13-17 skipped turns a battle) against both c and aa, gains vs c / vs aa (coverage/shards/locks.tsv):
#   gl (GUN-11 gun stack)        PhoenixOS +4.4 +- 2.3 vs mean(c, aa) (12) and +3.3 +- 3.3 on 12 more
#                                PinkPanther +1.6 +- 2.1 vs mean (24 at 0.7x), pooled with an earlier 24-seed block
#                                +2.2 +- 1.8; MatchupMini +1.1 +- 1.3 (24 at 0.7x), pooled with an earlier 24 +1.4 +- 1.1
#                                (we deal both far less than BB does: 898 to its 1,807 on PinkPanther)
#   cpl (COPY-2 bred gun copy)   Identity +2.2 / +2.7 (36) and +2.4 / +1.8 recheck (12); PumpkinPie +2.4 / +2.8 (24)
#                                and a recheck at +1.4 / +4.5 (12); both missed in round 33, so the PC reads them again
#   rwl (MOVE-46 ram wait)       Phoenix +2.3 / +2.2 recheck (12), +1.9 / +1.9 at 0.7x (missed in round 32 at +0.33)
#   dn (DIST-4, 400 px)          GresSuffurd +3.4 / +3.6 (36)
#   hof (MOVE-71 head-on floor)  Splooshlu +0.5 / +0.9 (24)
#   qw (MOVE-67 aim weight)      LevelOne +0.8 / +0.8 (12)
#   rlnrkn (RAM-20 and RAM-21)   SquidmanNano +1.8 / +1.3 (12), Ringo +1.2 / +1.4 (12)
#   rf (RAM-15 ram flee)         TrialBot +2.1 / +2.9 (24), +2.5 +- 0.8 vs mean(c, aa)
# Holden pads the A/A check (13 robots). The PC reads 24 fresh seeds from 115000 and a line
# ships only on the PC's own read.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: each line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - Diagnosis: PhoenixOS out-fires us at the same range (we fire 0.89 to its 1.11 and battles run long), where the gun
#     stack adds the second gun's view; the cpl robots hit us with learning guns that their bred copy reproduces;
#     Phoenix lands its hits after our endgame ram starts; GresSuffurd hits us more at its own preferred distance and a
#     400 px pin keeps us out of it; Splooshlu and LevelOne are head-on and simple-aim heavy; SquidmanNano and Ringo
#     ram, and the learned shot model plus the known-rammer start keep the escape on from the first scan; TrialBot's
#     learning gun lands its hits once it closes, and ram flee keeps the distance.
#   - Every line read positive against both controls at PC-like turn time on fresh cloud seeds; 24 PC seeds settle it.
#
# The turn-time check (skip, after the gate): master after TIME-14 and TIME-15 (sk) against master just before them
# (c and aa, built from d6f7c28 under their own names, plans/pc-skipcheck.arms) on 35 robots (panel-skipcheck.txt: the
# cloud skip-cost panel and six rammers on the learned escape path), 24 fresh seeds from 115100. Read: skipped turns
# and engine disables a battle per arm and per robot, and sk minus mean(c, aa) pooled and per band with the A/A
# (multiarm.py). The cloud expects skips -35% overall and -75 to -90% on the rammers, score +0.2 to +0.4 pooled; the
# score read is the gate, since after TIME-15 a skipped turn sheds no work and skip counts understate the gain.
#
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): no aa stop rule (aa is read in the gate). Each bench step halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24 or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live, in its
#              own folder (work/pc-locks35-livematch), so no earlier round's battle is read back
#   lock       panel-locks.txt  c / aa, 24 fresh seeds from 115000, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks35-ctl
#   stage      writes each lever's two-arm file (c and the lever) and copies in, times kept, the c battles of that lever's
#              own robots, so the bench reads them back (BENCH-95) and the watcher counts them as resumed
#   lock-X     each lever arm on its own picked robots only, same seeds, in work/pc-locks35-X; the gate takes c and aa
#              from -ctl and only the lever rows from each -X
#   gate       each robot judged on its own lever arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low
#              end is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0)
#   skip       c / aa / sk on panel-skipcheck.txt, 24 fresh seeds from 115100, in work/pc-locks35-skip; no skips stop
#              rule here, since skipped turns are what it measures and the pre-fix rammers may pass 60 a battle
#   skipread   multiarm.py (control c, A/A aa, live-field band weights), per_robot.py for sk, and skipped turns and
#              engine disables a battle per robot and arm
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 34 left this plan's queue state marked complete; the new work directory and seeds mean no
#   battle is read back from an earlier round (and BENCH-272 refights any whose jar changed).
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 124 live-match battles, 912 lock battles (13
# robots in c and aa, each lever robot again on its own arm, 24 seeds) and 2,520 skip-check battles (35 robots, 3 arms,
# 24 seeds): 3,556 in all, about 75 minutes (round 34's 3,672 took about 75).
# The prep step stops if any panel robot's jar is missing.
#
set V = 3.24
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks35
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && DIST_PIN=plans/skipcheck-dummy.list DIST_PIN_SUFFIX=pre bash ./build-ablation.sh --ref d6f7c28 dplist && DIST_PIN=plans/skipcheck-dummy.list DIST_PIN_SUFFIX=pra bash ./build-ablation.sh --ref d6f7c28 dplist && for a in pre pra; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in gl cpl rwl dn hof qw rlnrkn rf; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; awk -F"\t" -v a=$a '$2 == a {print $1 " |"}' plans/locks-pick.tsv > ${W}-prep/$a.names && grep -F -f ${W}-prep/$a.names panel-locks.txt > ${W}-prep/$a.panel && grep "^$a |" ${W}-prep/lock.arms > ${W}-prep/$a.arms || exit 1; done && grep -E "^(c|aa) [|]" ${W}-prep/lock.arms > ${W}-prep/ctl.arms && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-skipcheck.txt && for j in $(grep -hv "^#" panel-locks.txt panel-skipcheck.txt | cut -d"|" -f3); do test -f opponents/$j || { echo "missing jar $j"; exit 1; }; done && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out ${W}-livematch --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py ${W}-livematch/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks35-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/ctl.arms --out ${W}-ctl --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

stage | for a in gl cpl rwl dn hof qw rlnrkn rf; do grep -E "^(c|$a) [|]" ${W}-prep/lock.arms > ${W}-prep/$a-c.arms && mkdir -p ${W}-$a/battles || exit 1; for s in $(grep -v "^#" ${W}-prep/$a.panel | cut -d"|" -f1 | sed -E "s/^ +| +$//g; s/[^A-Za-z0-9.]+/_/g"); do cp -rp ${W}-ctl/battles/$s-*-c ${W}-$a/battles/ || exit 1; done; done
  after: lock

lock-gl | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/gl.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/gl-c.arms --out ${W}-gl --label pc-locks-gl --shuffle-jobs
  after: stage
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock-cpl | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/cpl.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/cpl-c.arms --out ${W}-cpl --label pc-locks-cpl --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-gl
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock-rwl | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/rwl.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/rwl-c.arms --out ${W}-rwl --label pc-locks-rwl --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-cpl
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock-dn | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/dn.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/dn-c.arms --out ${W}-dn --label pc-locks-dn --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-rwl
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock-hof | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/hof.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/hof-c.arms --out ${W}-hof --label pc-locks-hof --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-dn
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock-qw | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/qw.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/qw-c.arms --out ${W}-qw --label pc-locks-qw --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-hof
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock-rlnrkn | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/rlnrkn.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/rlnrkn-c.arms --out ${W}-rlnrkn --label pc-locks-rlnrkn --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-qw
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m
lock-rf | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set ${W}-prep/rf.panel --seeds 24 --seed-base 115000 --arms ${W}-prep/rf-c.arms --out ${W}-rf --label pc-locks-rf --shuffle-jobs
  after: lock-rlnrkn
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

gate | mkdir -p ${W} && (cat ${W}-ctl/arms.tsv && for d in gl cpl rwl dn hof qw rlnrkn rf; do awk -F"\t" -v a=$d 'NR > 1 && $1 == a' ${W}-$d/arms.tsv || exit 1; done) > ${W}/arms.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks35-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks35-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks35-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms gl cpl rwl dn hof qw rlnrkn rf --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks35-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks35-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock-rf

skip | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-skipcheck.txt --seeds 24 --seed-base 115100 --arms plans/pc-skipcheck.arms --out ${W}-skip --label pc-locks-skip --shuffle-jobs
  after: gate
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

skipread | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}-skip/arms.tsv --control c --aa aa --census census-live.txt --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks35-skip.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}-skip/arms.tsv --arms sk --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks35-skip-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks35-skip-per-robot.tsv && { printf "opponent\tarm\tbattles\tskips_per_battle\tdisables_per_battle\n"; awk -F"\t" 'NR == 1 {for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) h[$i] = i; next} $h["ok"] == "true" {k = $h["opponent"] "\t" $h["arm"]; n[k]++; s[k] += $h["skippedTurns"]; d[k] += $h["engineDisables"]} END {for (k in n) printf "%s\t%d\t%.1f\t%.2f\n", k, n[k], s[k] / n[k], d[k] / n[k]}' ${W}-skip/arms.tsv | sort; } > ${OUT}/pc-locks35-skip-load.tsv
  after: skip

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks35-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 35 (12 lines on gl, cpl, rwl, dn, hof, qw, rlnrkn, rf) and the turn-time check, 24 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks35-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks35-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks35-lock-per-robot.tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks35-skip-per-robot.tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks35-skip-load.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks35-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: skipread
